Hoisted the vector size and data pointer out of the loop so the scan avoids repeated `size()`/`operator[]` work on the vector object. This keeps the same first-match semantics while giving the compiler a simpler pointer/index loop.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    Field* const data = fields.data();
    const auto count = fields.size();
    for (decltype(fields.size()) i = 0; i < count; ++i)
    {
        if (data[i].GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return &data[i];
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```